From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: starfive: negotiate NV12 for desktop camera clients

Plain V4L2 clients select a capture size without configuring subdevices.
Previously S_FMT changed only the buffer layout, leaving the ISP source
at its initial size. GNOME Camera then failed STREAMON with EPIPE.

For the processed NV12 node, constrain TRY_FMT to the active ISP input
and apply the matching even Bayer-phase crop during S_FMT. Advertise
only sizes that this crop path can produce, and forward frame interval
queries and changes to the active sensor. TRY_FMT never modifies the
active graph. Keep the raw node's explicit media-controller interface.

Expose the mux inputs through ENUMINPUT/G_INPUT/S_INPUT so users can
select either camera with ordinary V4L2 tools while capture is idle.
Read the selected input from the enabled links, preserving compatibility
with media-controller tools. Propagate the selected sensor's Bayer mode
through the complete graph and restore the previous route on failure.

This uses the kernel ISP through the stock PipeWire V4L2 backend and does
not depend on a locally modified libcamera pipeline handler. It does not
turn on the board's flash LED, which is separate from camera streaming.

Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI)
